Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?sycl:=20B60/Xe2=20decode=20tuning=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20ESIMD=20weight=20prefetch=20+=20weight-streaming=20loads?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two independently gated kernel changes for batch-1 decode on Arc B60
(BMG-G21, Xe2), both default OFF:

1. GGML_SYCL_BMG_PREFETCH: in the reordered ESIMD dequant-matvec loop,
   issue an LSC prefetch (cached L1/L2) for the next iteration's weight
   blocks (qs + scales) so their DRAM latency overlaps the current
   block's dequant, raising outstanding-request count to better saturate
   the bandwidth-bound decode. Q4_K path.

2. GGML_SYCL_BMG_STREAM_W: route the reordered ESIMD weight loads through
   cache hints L1 uncached + L2 cached (frees L1 for activations, keeps
   L2 weight reuse).

Both target the Q4_K decode hot path (ESIMD reorder matvec, the
first-priority kernel for batch-1). Enable via -DGGML_SYCL_BMG_PREFETCH=ON
and/or -DGGML_SYCL_BMG_STREAM_W=ON.
---
